1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,016
Narrator: Scenario 28. Network and access.

2
00:00:05,616 --> 00:00:16,176
A: The shared service credential is due for rotation next week. Have we identified every consumer, including background jobs that might run less frequently?

3
00:00:16,776 --> 00:00:27,168
B: Three applications are confirmed. A monthly reconciliation job may also use it, but its owner has not verified the current configuration yet.

4
00:00:27,768 --> 00:00:39,168
C: We should resolve that uncertainty before revocation. Does the provider support two active credentials so we can migrate consumers without an immediate shared cutover?

5
00:00:39,768 --> 00:00:50,784
A: It supports two active credentials with separate identifiers. I propose creating the replacement in the approved secret store and tracking migration by consumer.

6
00:00:51,384 --> 00:01:01,728
B: The reconciliation owner just confirmed the job uses this account. We can run its validation mode today without posting any financial updates.

7
00:01:02,328 --> 00:01:15,120
C: Good. Record the credential identifier and test result, never the secret itself. Please also verify that the replacement has the same approved permission scope.

8
00:01:15,720 --> 00:01:27,264
A: I will check permissions and update one application first through the change process. We will observe authentication errors and completed transactions before migrating the others.

9
00:01:27,864 --> 00:01:36,696
B: How will we know the monthly job is no longer using the old credential? Its next scheduled run is after the rotation deadline.

10
00:01:37,296 --> 00:01:48,312
A: We will validate its updated secret reference and run the approved validation mode. Provider audit logs should show the replacement identifier for that execution.

11
00:01:48,912 --> 00:02:00,360
C: Do not revoke based only on silence in the logs. Require an explicit successful test from all four consumers and owner confirmation of the inventory.

12
00:02:00,960 --> 00:02:12,456
B: I will collect the application and job evidence by 17:00 UTC tomorrow. Any failed test will block revocation and trigger a review of the migration.

13
00:02:13,056 --> 00:02:23,664
A: After security approves the evidence, I will revoke the old credential and repeat key checks. We will then update the rotation schedule and ownership record.
